    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics feels like a dense forest to me—beautiful from afar but overwhelming when I try to navigate it. My parents, both PhDs, made it seem essential, but it never clicked like history or literature. I respect its precision, yet I avoid it like a chore, even though I know it’s foundational for so many fields. It’s frustrating, honestly, because I want to understand but often feel like I’m missing the map.",
